; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.336
;; What TS 29.336's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: S6m's and S6n's procedure (clause 5), common aspects,
;; commands, result codes and AVPs (clause 6), then S6t's (clauses 7 and 8).
;; SIR and SIA print once under 16777310 for S6m and S6n alike, SIR-Flags'
;; S6m/S6n Indicator telling the MTC-IWF's request from the MTC-AAA's; S6t's
;; commands print once under 16777345, NIR and NIA serving both directions.
;; A rule depending on a node, a feature, the subscription, what the HSS
;; stores or an earlier message is `text-only`.


;; Clause 5.2.1.1's tables. The IMSI is the User-Identifier's User-Name
;; (table 6.4.1/2); "exactly one" is read as at least one of the three and no
;; two, LMSI, an answer's identity, not among them.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-user-identifier-one
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This is a grouped AVP containing either an External Identifier, an MSISDN or an IMSI (exactly one, and only one, of those identifiers shall be included in the request)."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name or User-Identifier/MSISDN or User-Identifier/External-Identifier
    excludes User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/MSISDN or User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/External-Identifier or User-Identifier/MSISDN and User-Identifier/External-Identifier


;; S6n's request is the MTC-AAA's, which clears SIR-Flags' S6m/S6n
;; Indicator (table 6.4.10/1).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-service-id-s6n
; AVP: Service-ID
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


;; Clause 6.4.4's TBCD-string with no nature of address or numbering plan;
;; the two services are every Service-ID value, so every SCS-Identity is one
;; of theirs.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-scs-identity
; AVP: SCS-Identity
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the Service-ID indicates DEVICE_TRIGGER (0) or SMS_MO (1), the SCS-Identity shall be formatted as an E.164 address as described in clause 6.4.4."
"In this release, only the Device Triggering and SMS_MO services are supported."
    encoding e164-tbcd
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-service-parameters-s6n
; AVP: Service-Parameters
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


;; Each answer's Result row: the interface's errors are 3GPP's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for S6m/S6n errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-user-identifier-success
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present only when the Result- Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-service-data
; AVP: Service-Data
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present only when the Requested Service IE was included in the request, and the Result- Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires request/Service-ID and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; Clause 5.2.1.2, the HSS: what the subscription holds; an S6n request,
;; its S6m/S6n Indicator clear, answered with success carries the user's
;; identities. Step 4's Serving-Node left out for an absent user is clause
;; 6.4.8's rule, read there.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-user-identifier-returned
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"if available, the MSISDN of the user shall also be returned by the HSS, along with the user's IMSI."
    text-only
"If it is known, the HSS shall answer successfully and return in the response one or several instances of the User Identity IE, each one containing either an External-Identifier or an MSISDN (if any of these identities are present in the subscriber profile in HSS), or the subscriber's IMSI (if the subscriber does not have any External Identifiers or MSISDNs assigned)."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


;; Clauses 5.2.1.3 and 5.2.1.4: which node sends the request only the bit
;; itself shows.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-flags-mtc-iwf
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.3
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the MTC-IWF sends a Subscriber Information Retrieval request to the HSS, it shall set the S6m/S6n indicator bit in the SIR Flags IE."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-flags-mtc-aaa
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the MTC-AAA sends a Subscriber Information Retrieval request to the HSS, it shall clear the S6m/S6n indicator bit in the SIR Flags IE."
    text-only


;; The MTC-AAA's request, its S6m/S6n Indicator clear, holds the IMSI and
;; no other identifier; the other IEs its table makes absent for S6n are read
;; at the table, its SIR-Flags the ABNF requires.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-user-identifier-mtc-aaa
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The MTC-AAA shall only include the User Identifier IE in the request, and it shall contain only the IMSI of the UE."
    requires SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" or User-Identifier/User-Name
    excludes not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/MSISDN or not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/External-Identifier or not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/LMSI


;; Clause 6.1.4, the use of sessions, in S6m's and S6n's two commands: the
;; clause opens on the MTC-IWF and the HSS, and the client and server of its
;; requirement are the application's, the MTC-AAA's request one print with the
;; MTC-IWF's. The two AVPs RFC 6733 defines are admitted through each body's
;; * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


;; Clause 6.1.9, in each command carrying the AVP. TS 29.229 clause 6.3.29 has a
;; vendor's own features carry its own Vendor-Id, and which list a
;; Supported-Features carries only its Vendor-Id and Feature-List-ID tell, so
;; whether one is the document's own the message does not say.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-supported-features-vendor
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.9
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-supported-features-vendor
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.9
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only


;; Clause 6.2.2, in each command, as TS 29.338's clause 5.3.2.2: a rule on
;; the sender's: the receiver ignores the AVP, and the NOTE has the
;; command formats print it for intermediate agents not complying with
;; RFC 6733, so a capture past such an agent may hold it rightly.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-no-vendor-specific-application-id
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP shall not be included in any command sent by Diameter nodes supporting applications defined in this specification."
"If the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP is received in any of the commands defined in this specification, it shall be ignored by the receiving node."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-no-vendor-specific-application-id
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP shall not be included in any command sent by Diameter nodes supporting applications defined in this specification."
"If the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP is received in any of the commands defined in this specification, it shall be ignored by the receiving node."
    text-only


;; Clause 6.3.3, in the answer, the three codes its clauses define, TS
;; 29.229's DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN (5001) among them.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sia-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.3.3
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and the Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415 and Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code in DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN,
        DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_REQUESTING_ENTITY,
        DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_SERVICE
    exclude 5510, 5511


;; Clause 6.4.2's AVPs. The identifiers are the four members its body
;; names. Which member carries the IMSI, "when applicable", says what it
;; holds, not a rule.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-identifier-not-empty
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Section: 6.4.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This AVP shall contain at least one of the identifiers used by the UE, i.e., it shall not be empty."
    members at-least-one User-Name MSISDN External-Identifier LMSI


;; Teleservice Not Provisioned's and Call Barred's "should not be
;; present" is no requirement.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: t4-data-serving-node-absent-subscriber
; AVP: Serving-Node
; Within: T4-Data
; Section: 6.4.8
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS-Cause indicates Absent Subscriber, via the corresponding flag in the bit mask, the Serving-Node and Additional-Serving-Node AVPs shall not be present."
    absent-if HSS-Cause bit "Absent Subscriber"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: t4-data-additional-serving-node
; AVP: Additional-Serving-Node
; Within: T4-Data
; Section: 6.4.8
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS-Cause indicates Absent Subscriber, via the corresponding flag in the bit mask, the Serving-Node and Additional-Serving-Node AVPs shall not be present."
    absent-if HSS-Cause bit "Absent Subscriber"
"Additional-Serving-Node AVP shall be absent if Serving-Node AVP is absent."
    requires Serving-Node


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: hss-cause-undefined-bits
; AVP: HSS-Cause
; Section: 6.4.9
; Table: 6.4.9/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"NOTE 2: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the HSS and discarded by the receiving node, MTC-IWF."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sir-flags-undefined-bits
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Section: 6.4.10
; Table: 6.4.10/1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Note: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sending node, MTC-IWF or MTC-AAA, and discarded by the receiving HSS."
    bits only 0


;; Which of TS 23.003's identifiers the AVP carries turns on the
;; interface, an S6t one being a UE's (clause 19.7.2) or a group's (19.7.3) as
;; Type-Of-External-Identifier says, and no element can name both; each is a
;; username@realm or groupname@realm, a text no codec or shape reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: external-identifier-format
; AVP: External-Identifier
; Section: 6.4.11
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6m/S6n interface it shall contain an external identifier of the UE. See 3GPP TS 23.003 [11] for the definition and formatting of the External Identifier. For S6t interface, it shall contain an external identifier for an individual UE or a group of UEs, as indicated by Type-Of-External-Identifier AVP."
    text-only


;; The combinations clause 6.4.12 allows, read member by member as TS
;; 29.338's clause 5.3.3.6 is: every one holds one of the four numbers, and
;; each member only beside the others of its combination. Combination b's
;; condition is the HSS's, which the AVP does not show, so its members are
;; allowed whatever it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-number
; AVP: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"d) MSC-Number"
"f) IP-SM-GW-Number"
    members at-least-one SGSN-Number MME-Number-for-MT-SMS MSC-Number IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-sgsn-number
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    excludes MME-Name or MME-Realm or MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MSC-Number or IP-SM-GW-Number or IP-SM-GW-Name or IP-SM-GW-Realm


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-sgsn-name
; AVP: SGSN-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Realm and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-sgsn-realm
; AVP: SGSN-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Name and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-mme-name
; AVP: MME-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Realm and MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MME-Realm and MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-mme-realm
; AVP: MME-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Name


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-mme-number
; AVP: MME-Number-for-MT-SMS
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
    requires MME-Name and MME-Realm
    excludes MSC-Number or IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-msc-number
; AVP: MSC-Number
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"d) MSC-Number"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    excludes IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-ip-sm-gw-name
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"g) IP-SM-GW-Number & IP-SM-GW-Name & IP-SM-GW-Realm"
    requires IP-SM-GW-Number and IP-SM-GW-Realm


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: serving-node-ip-sm-gw-realm
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"g) IP-SM-GW-Number & IP-SM-GW-Name & IP-SM-GW-Realm"
    requires IP-SM-GW-Number and IP-SM-GW-Name


;; As Serving-Node's, its five combinations.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-number
; AVP: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"d) MSC-Number"
    members at-least-one SGSN-Number MME-Number-for-MT-SMS MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-sgsn-number
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    excludes MME-Name or MME-Realm or MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-sgsn-name
; AVP: SGSN-Name
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Realm and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-sgsn-realm
; AVP: SGSN-Realm
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Name and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-mme-name
; AVP: MME-Name
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Realm and MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MME-Realm and MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-mme-realm
; AVP: MME-Realm
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Name


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: additional-serving-node-mme-number
; AVP: MME-Number-for-MT-SMS
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
    requires MME-Name and MME-Realm
    excludes MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ip-sm-gw-number-e164
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Number
; Section: 6.4.14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The IP-SM-GW-Number AVP is of type OctetString and it shall contain the ISDN number of the IP-SM-GW in international number format as described in ITU-T Rec E.164 [41]. It shall be encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP shall not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan."
    encoding e164-tbcd


;; Clause 7.2.1.1's tables. Whether an External-Identifier names a
;; group the User-Identifier's Type-Of-External-Identifier says, which its
;; * [ AVP ] admits as clause 8.4.36's S6t format prints it, its absence an
;; individual UE's identity.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-user-identifier-one
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This is a grouped AVP containing either an External Identifier or an MSISDN (exactly one, and only one, of those identifiers shall be included in the request)."
    requires User-Identifier/External-Identifier or User-Identifier/MSISDN
    excludes User-Identifier/External-Identifier and User-Identifier/MSISDN


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-group-reporting-guard-timer
; AVP: Group-Reporting-Guard-Timer
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Shall be present if the User-Identifier contains an External Group Identifier."
    present-if User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE


;; A request's purpose its own AVP's presence tells.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-additional-identifiers
; AVP: AdditionalIdentifiers
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the request is used to retrieve multiple IMSI Group IDs for multiple External Group Identifiers, this information element shall be present and shall contain all the External Group Identifiers for which the IMSI Group IDs are requested, except the one conveyed in the User-Identifier AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall only be used for S6t errors which are applicable regardless of the services requested (e.g. DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN). This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-user-identifier
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall not be present if the External-Identifier of User-Identifier in CIR message contains the identity of a Group of UEs (i.e. External Group Identifier). This IE shall be present only when the Result-Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    absent-if request/User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; Held to a success's answer; the table prints Number-of-UEs for the
;; AVP its ABNF names Number-Of-UEs.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-number-of-ues
; AVP: Number-Of-UEs
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present if the External-Identifier of User-Identifier in CIR message contains the identity of a Group of UEs (i.e. External Group Identifier)."
    present-if request/User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; What the HSS has available.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-monitoring-event-report
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If an immediate report is available this information element shall contain the requested data available in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-monitoring-event-config-status
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Config-Status
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present if Monitoring Event Configuration IE is included in CIR and if the Result-Code AVP in Configuration Information Answer is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if request/Monitoring-Event-Configuration and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; What the HSS stores.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-s6t-hss-cause
; AVP: S6t-HSS-Cause
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"It shall be present if the user is not registered in any serving node."
    text-only


;; Held to a success's answer, where the row says nothing of an error's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-enhanced-coverage-restriction-data
; AVP: Enhanced-Coverage-Restriction-Data
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"It shall be present if the request contained a CIR-Flag AVP with the bit for Enhanced-Coverage-Query set."
    present-if request/CIR-Flags bit "Enhanced Coverage Query" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-imsi-group-id
; AVP: IMSI-Group-Id
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This information element shall be present if the CIR-Flag for IMSI Group Retrieval was set in the request and the Result-Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if request/CIR-Flags bit "IMSI Group Id retrieval" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; Clause 7.2.1.2, the HSS. A new monitoring event is a
;; Monitoring-Event-Configuration holding a reference ID, which the receiving
;; node stores, where one holding only a reference ID for deletion deletes: a
;; path into the AVP, any one of the request's holding one.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-delete-all-monitoring-events
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"IF the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all monitoring events, the HSS shall delete all Monitoring events configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes forwarding the deletion to involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new monitoring events."
    absent-if CIR-Flags bit "Delete all Monitoring events" and Monitoring-Event-Configuration/SCEF-Reference-ID or CIR-Flags bit "Delete all Monitoring events" and Monitoring-Event-Configuration/SCEF-Reference-ID-Ext


;; A feature both nodes support.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-delete-all-communication-pattern
; AVP: AESE-Communication-Pattern
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all communication pattern, and the feature Config-Eff-CP is supported, the HSS shall delete all Communication Pattern configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes forwarding the deletion to involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new communication pattern."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-delete-all-network-parameter-configurations
; AVP: Suggested-Network-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all network parameter configurations, and the feature Config-Eff-NP is supported, the HSS shall delete all Suggested Network Configurations configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes the updating of involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new network parameter configurations."
    text-only


;; What the HSS decided.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-suggested-network-configuration-unmodified
; AVP: Suggested-Network-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS did not modify parameters received in the Suggested-Network-Configuration AVP, the HSS shall return a Suggested-Network-Configuration AVP to the SCEF in CIA containing only SCEF Reference ID and SCEF-ID."
    text-only


;; Clause 7.2.2.1's tables. The HSS sends every RIR to the SCEF; whether
;; a report is the group's configuration processing the request does not
;; show.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-user-identifier
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This AVP shall not carry the IMSI towards the SCEF."
    excludes User-Identifier/User-Name
"For group based configuration processing, the External-Identifier shall be present and contain an External Group Identifier (see 3GPP TS 23.003 [11])."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-monitoring-event-report
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If a report is available in the HSS this information element shall contain the requested data available in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-group-report
; AVP: Group-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Shall be present if User-Identifier contains an External Group Identifier"
    present-if User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-supported-services
; AVP: Supported-Services
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If RIR-flags indicates a change of SCEF authorization for one or more monitoring events, this information element shall be present."
    present-if RIR-Flags bit Change-Of-Authorized-Monitoring-Events


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for S6t errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 7.2.2.2, the HSS: what it knows, what triggered the request,
;; and features both nodes support.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-group-configuration-in-progress
; AVP: RIR-Flags
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the HSS knows that it has additional RIR commands to send for the same group, the HSS shall include the RIR-Flags AVP with the Group-Configuration-In-Progress bit set and restart the Group Guard Timer to the value it originally received in the CIR."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-report-eff-monte
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the HSS and SCEF support the Report-Eff-MONTE feature, the HSS shall make use of RIR-flags AVP for a given User-Identity and no Monitoring-Event-Report AVP(s) shall be included."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: group-report-item-partially-cancel
; AVP: S6t-HSS-Cause
; Within: Group-Report-Item
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the RIR command is triggered by partially cancelling of group-based monitoring, the S6t-HSS-Cause IE shall be set to \"Group Event Monitoring Partially Cancel\"."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: supported-services-node-type
; AVP: Node-Type
; Within: Supported-Services
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the services supported and authorized by the HSS are the same than those supported by the serving node(s), the Node-Type AVP shall be absent."
    text-only


;; Clause 7.2.3.1's tables. The SCEF's authorization request carries the
;; NIDD-Authorization-Request, absent from the HSS's, and the HSS's update the
;; NIDD-Authorization-Update, absent from the SCEF's. That the SCEF's holds one
;; of the two identifiers is not read: clause 7.2.3.2's step 6 has its
;; User-Identifier contain an IMSI, NOTE 2 a T6a/b CMR's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nir-user-identifier
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This is a grouped AVP containing in authorization requests sent from SCEF to HSS either an External Identifier or an MSISDN (exactly one, and only one, of those identifiers shall be included in the request), and containing in update/revocation requests sent from HSS to SCEF an IMSI and either MSISDN or External Identifier or both."
    excludes NIDD-Authorization-Request and User-Identifier/External-Identifier and User-Identifier/MSISDN
    requires not NIDD-Authorization-Update or User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/MSISDN or User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/External-Identifier


;; Only the SCEF sends it, so it always holds the APN.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nir-nidd-authorization-request
; AVP: NIDD-Authorization-Request
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When sent by the SCEF, the Service-Selection AVP inside NIDD-Authorization-Request shall be present, and it shall contain the APN for which NIDD authorization is requested. Shall be absent when sent by the HSS."
    members at-least-one Service-Selection


;; The HSS's alone, where NIDD-Authorization-Request's row has that AVP
;; the SCEF's alone.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nir-nidd-authorization-update
; AVP: NIDD-Authorization-Update
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If present, this Information Element shall contain the details of the updated NIDD Authorization. Shall be absent when sent by the SCEF."
"Shall be absent when sent by the HSS."
    excludes NIDD-Authorization-Request


;; An earlier answer.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nir-group-user-identifier
; AVP: Group-User-Identifier
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-1
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This information element shall be present if the request is sent from HSS to SCEF following a previous NIA with an incomplete Group User Identifier List."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nia-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: NIDD-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for S6t errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; The SCEF sends none, so where present the answer is the HSS's; the
;; SCEF's answers the HSS's update, its request's NIDD-Authorization-Update.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nia-nidd-authorization-response
; AVP: NIDD-Authorization-Response
; Command: NIDD-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When sent by the HSS the IE shall only be present when the Result Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS. Shall be absent when sent by the SCEF."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
    absent-if request/NIDD-Authorization-Update


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nia-group-user-identifier
; AVP: Group-User-Identifier
; Command: NIDD-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.3.1
; Table: 7.2.3.1-2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This information element shall be present if the request was for a group of UEs and the Result-Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if request/User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; Clause 7.2.3.2, the HSS's answer to the SCEF's request. An External
;; Identifier may be a group's, whose IMSIs step 6a puts in the
;; Group-User-Identifier; an MSISDN is one UE's, whose IMSI the response's
;; User-Name carries (clause 8.4.45). What the subscription holds, and two
;; times compared, no kind says.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nia-nidd-authorization-response-identities
; AVP: NIDD-Authorization-Response
; Command: NIDD-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.3.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"4. If the User-Identifier contains an External Identifier, the HSS shall include the IMSI and if available the MSISDN associated with the appropriate External Identifier in the NIDD-Authorization-Response."
    text-only
"5. If the User-Identifier contains an MSISDN, the HSS shall include the IMSI and if available, the appropriate External Identifier associated with the MSISDN in the NIDD-Authorization-Response."
    requires not request/User-Identifier/MSISDN or NIDD-Authorization-Response/User-Name
"6. If the User-Identifier contains an IMSI the HSS shall include the MSISDN and the appropriate External Identifier assigned to the IMSI in the NIDD-Authorization-Response."
    text-only
"The HSS may indicate within the NIDD-Authorization-Response AVP a granted validity time which shall not be later than the requested validity time as received within the NIDD-Authorization-Request AVP (if any)."
    text-only


;; Each Group-User-Identifier is one member's, in the first NIA or a
;; later NIR alike; table 7.2.3.1-2 says it again of the NIA.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: group-user-identifier-member
; AVP: Group-User-Identifier
; Section: 7.2.3.2
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"6a. If the User-Identifier contains an External Group Identifier, the HSS shall include the IMSI and the MSISDN or External-Identifier assigned to each member of the group in the Group-User-Identifier."
    members at-least-one User-Name
    members at-least-one MSISDN External-Identifier


;; Clause 8.1.4, the use of sessions, in each S6t command; the two AVPs
;; RFC 6733 defines are admitted through each body's * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cir-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 8.1.4
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


