"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


;; Clause 8.1.6: the RIR's body requires both; the HSS's NIR is told
;; apart by its NIDD-Authorization-Update (table 7.2.3.1-1), the segments it
;; sends of a Group User Identifier List by nothing the request shows.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nir-hss-destination-host
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.6
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"As the HSS knows the address/name and the associated home network domain name of the SCEF to which it sends RIR and NIR commands from a previously received CIR command, both the Destination-Realm and Destination-Host AVPs shall be present in request commands sent by the HSS to the SCEF."
    present-if NIDD-Authorization-Update


;; Clause 8.1.9, as clause 6.1.9 for S6m and S6n.
